#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY Change delivery"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Every change is reviewed with its plan and applied by CI only, after merge."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: delivery · depends on: [CAP-CIIDENTITY]{1}, [CAP-STATE]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Make every change to a shared environment reviewed, visible as a plan, and applied by one writer."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "One writer gives one audit trail and real locking ([P1]{1}). Deletion through code keeps the record of what was removed and why. Migrating the database before deploying the code that needs it avoids a release that cannot run."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Change review showing the plan artefact."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Apply stage consuming that artefact after merge, or by dispatch for trust anchors."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Version tags as the only release trigger."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "When CI lacks a right, give CI's identity the right in one documented bootstrap step. A workstation apply is a second writer, not a shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Every change to infrastructure or a shared environment, including grants, migrations and deletions, is a reviewed change whose plan is shown in the review."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Sample merged changes; each carries the plan CI produced for it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Only CI applies. Apply recipes refuse to run anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Run an apply recipe on a workstation; it refuses before contacting any API."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CI applies the saved plan that was reviewed, not a fresh one."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "The apply step consumes the plan artefact produced by the plan step."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "A trust-anchor change is dispatched by hand from the main branch by an allow-listed role, after approval by both the Data Lead and the Technical Lead."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "The bootstrap pipeline checks the actor against its allow-list before any credential is issued; its environment requires two approvals."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "A deletion is two changes: adopt the object into code, then remove it.{1}*Example:* To remove an unused storage account, one reviewed change imports it into code and the next deletes it, so the removal is planned and reviewed like any other change."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Every removal of a resource in history is preceded by a change that imported it or created it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "A database is migrated before the code that needs it is deployed; a release is a version tag, and an infrastructure change alone never changes what version runs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Pipeline order runs migrations first; deployments take the image version from a tag."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "A scheduled fitness check fails if any state was written by an identity other than CI."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "The check reads the last writer of each state version and alerts on a non-CI principal."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "CAP-DELIVERY.8"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Every deployable artefact carries SLSA v1.2 Build Level 3 provenance and a software bill of materials in SPDX 2.3 or later or CycloneDX 1.5 or later."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-delivery.md
msgid "Release artefacts include a provenance attestation and an SBOM that validate."
msgstr ""

